{"collection":{"version":"1.1","href":"http://images-api.nasa.gov/search?q=PREFIRE+launch&media_type=image&page=1","items":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/KSC-20240605-PH-RKL01_0003/collection.json","data":[{"album":["Rocket_Lab_PREFIRE"],"center":"KSC","date_created":"2024-06-05T00:00:00Z","description":"Rocket Lab’s Electron rocket called “PREFIRE and Ice,” is vertical on the pad awaiting liftoff at Launch Complex 1 in Mahia, New Zealand, ahead of NASA’s PREFIRE (Polar Radiant Energy in the Far-InfraRed Experiment) mission Wednesday, June 5, 2024. The mission, the second of two launches for NASA’S PREFIRE, features two identical 6U CubeSats in asynchronous, near-polar orbits, will study how much of Earth’s heat is lost to space from the Arctic and Antarctica. ","keywords":["NASA","PREFIRE","Polar Radiant Energy in the Far InfraRed Experiment","LSP","Launch Services Program","JPL","Jet Propulsion Laboratory","Earth","climate","CubeSat","small satellite","sea ice","melting","global warming","arctic","tropics","poles","Rocket Lab","Electron","New Zealand","Ready Aim PREFIRE","PREFIRE and Ice"],"location":"Launch Complex 1, New Zealand","media_type":"image","nasa_id":"KSC-20240605-PH-RKL01_0003","photographer":"Rocket Lab","title":"Rocket Lab PREFIRE and Ice Launch"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/KSC-20240605-PH-RKL01_0003/KSC-20240605-PH-RKL01_0003~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":853,"size":64000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/KSC-20240605-PH-RKL01_0003/KSC-20240605-PH-RKL01_0003~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":426,"size":21000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/KSC-20240605-PH-RKL01_0003/KSC-20240605-PH-RKL01_0003~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":426,"size":21000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/KSC-20240605-PH-RKL01_0003/KSC-20240605-PH-RKL01_0003~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","rend